{"annotationDigest":"sha256:6288ff18184917fc8541df34afde309789c00132a2bfc915b07b43d4fff648ff","annotationId":"rann-5f860ea3882dabbad2c594326bf95e82","author":{"agent":"claude-code","kind":"ai","model":"claude-opus-5.5"},"createdAt":"2026-09-29T07:58:33Z","disclaimer":"AI-generated review opinion derived from the evidence package. It is not a verdict, does not change readiness, and must be confirmed by a human reviewer.","disclosureCheck":{"blocking":46,"contradictions":[],"disclosures":51,"nextDecision":"human_judgement","readiness":"blocked"},"findings":[{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:stripJsonc","SW-REQ-260927-66FW"],"scenario":"parseMenuJsonc on an object whose last entry ends with a comma followed by a full-line // comment and then } (e.g. the shipped user extension template with its Examples uncommented)"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"Reproduced locally with node against the evaluated MenuModel.js (and byte-identically against the upstream head f75205f9 stripJsonc): the input `{\\n \"a\": {\"label\": \"A\"},\\n // trailing note\\n}` parses to 1 row at the baseline and to [] with this change. Cause: comments are no longer removed BEFORE the comma pass; the comma lookahead at MenuModel.js:31-32 skips whitespace only, sees `/`, keeps the comma, then the comment is dropped and JSON.parse rejects `{...,}` - the catch in parseMenuJsonc returns an empty set. The shipped user template config/omarchy/extensions/omarchy-menu.jsonc hits this exactly when a user uncomments its Examples (lines 20-22): baseline 3 rows, this change 0 rows. A comma followed by an inline comment then `}` fails both before and after. Suggested fix: make the comma lookahead also skip `//...\\n` runs (or strip comments string-aware first, then commas). None of the new witnesses covers comma-then-comment. The engine cannot settle this from static facts; a test must.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":31},{"id":"config/omarchy/extensions/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":22},{"id":"SW-REQ-260927-66FW","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-E4J2","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"high","title":"Question: does a trailing comma followed by a comment line before } now empty the whole menu?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Trailing comma, then a full-line comment, then }\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js:stripJsonc","SW-REQ-260928-C8W1"],"scenario":"parseMenuJsonc on a value split by an inline comment with no whitespace, e.g. '{\"a\": {\"label\": \"A\", \"n\": 1//c\\n2}}' - must it fail rather than read n=12?"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The comment loop at MenuModel.js:28 stops ON the newline and the for-loop increment then skips it, so the newline is dropped too. `[1//c\\n2]` becomes `[12]`: input that was invalid JSONC (missing comma) now parses to a different value instead of failing. The baseline full-line regex also consumed its newline, but only for whole-line comments where the previous line's newline survives. Bounded consequence (malformed input only), but a one-character fix (stop before the newline, keep it) removes it.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":28},{"id":"SW-REQ-260928-C8W1","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: can dropping the comment's newline join two tokens into a different valid value?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Comment between two tokens without whitespace does not join them\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"review.diffCoverage was measured (mcdc bash+js): 6/6 chan