inding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:1029b355c7359f7e28bd1c50db0ac51a774c57d93aeaa31a76ef2a304cf88c08","packageIdentity":"epkg-21d410a14a02b83c290c6f41893f1c1d38cdcb3521340c3295ce110c2291c589","riskAssessment":{"level":"high","rationale":"Engine risk is high and readiness blocked (introduced). A locally reproduced comma-then-comment case that parsed at baseline now empties the menu; it needs a test."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":0,"rationale":"assertEqual(menu.parseMenuJsonc('{\\n \"a\": {\"label\": \"A\"},\\n // note\\n}').length, 1) - fails on this change, passes at baseline; also parse the shipped extension template with its Examples uncommented (expect 3 rows).","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":31},{"id":"config/omarchy/extensions/omarchy-menu.jsonc","kind":"file","line":22}],"title":"Trailing comma, then a full-line comment, then }"},{"forClaim":1,"rationale":"'{\"a\": {\"label\": \"A\", \"n\": 1//c\\n2}}' should yield [] (invalid), not n=12.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/MenuModel.js","kind":"file","line":28}],"title":"Comment between two tokens without whitespace does not join them"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Fixes #13493: an inline `//` tail (`{...} // note`) survived the line-anchored comment regex, JSON.parse failed and the menu went empty. Comment stripping is folded into the string-aware scanner from #13255 (upstream is stacked on it). Our stripJsonc is code-identical to upstream head f75205f9; C8W1, witnesses and the review/ reproducer are dogfood proof work.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Changed-code coverage was measured: 0 uncovered lines/outcomes in stripJsonc; the inline-tail and `\"A // B\"` rows exercise the new branch. Test outcomes are not observed in this package (test_outcome_unobserved), so this is coverage, not a pass record.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) Reproduced locally: a trailing comma followed by a comment line before `}` parsed at baseline and now yields an empty menu, because the comma lookahead sees `/` not `}` - the shipped user template does this when its Examples are uncommented. Needs a test and likely a fix. (2) The comment loop also drops the newline, so `1//c\\n2` reads as `12`.\n\n**Traceability.** C8W1 added; 66FW's 'next non-whitespace character' wording should say 'non-comment'. Effects analysis is unavailable for JS. The three review/ reproducer candidates are argued noise.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** Readiness is blocked (introduced): missing_obligation:C8W1 and check_regressed:spec_lint_hazard_review_current (C8W1 hazard review) are new; suspect_clean, verify_passes, orphan_code_clean, process_checklist and nine other missing obligations are inherited. The next decision is a policy approver's judgement on policy_changed_unclassified."}
